# Walkthrough: Website Successfully Deployed! 🚀

I have successfully deployed your **Coolex Shop** to the internet using a **Cloudflare Quick Tunnel**. Your PC is now acting as a secure web server.

## 🌐 Public Link
You can access your website from anywhere in the world using this URL:

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Primary URL:** [https://become-editorial-directive-certification.trycloudflare.com/coolex_shop/](https://become-editorial-directive-certification.trycloudflare.com/coolex_shop/)

*Note: Since your local site is in the `/coolex_shop/` folder, you must include it in the URL.*

---

## 🛠️ How it was Setup
1.  **Downloaded `cloudflared.exe`**: I downloaded the official Cloudflare tool to your project's `bin/` folder.
2.  **Verified Local Server**: Confirmed that UniServerZ was active on **Port 81**.
3.  **Initialized Tunnel**: Started a secure background process that bridges your local `localhost:81` to the public `trycloudflare.com` domain.

---

## ⚠️ Important Maintenance Notes

### 1. Keeping the Site Online
For your website to stay accessible, two things must remain running on your PC:
1.  **UniServerZ (Apache & MySQL)**
2.  **The Cloudflare Tunnel Process**

If you restart your PC, you will need to restart the tunnel. You can do this by opening a PowerShell window in your project folder and running:
```powershell
.\bin\cloudflared.exe tunnel --url http://localhost:81
```

### 2. Temporary URL
Since we don't have a domain name yet, this URL is **temporary**. If the tunnel process is stopped and restarted, a new random URL will be generated.

> [!TIP]
> **Want a Permanent Site?**
> If you decide to get a domain (e.g., `.com`), I can help you link it to Cloudflare so your URL never changes.

### 3. Verification
I have confirmed the tunnel process is currently running and healthy in your background tasks.
